  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Fca Us has $512M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Fca Us won 11,836 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $43.3K. Obligations are up 101.5% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations show pronounced swings: FY21 totaled $267M, FY22 totaled $16.1M, FY23 totaled $356M, FY24 totaled $330M, FY25 totaled $254M, and FY26 totaled $512M. The current-year total is partial, covering fiscal year to date activity. The award count and average award size indicate a high-volume, relatively small-award profile in the current fiscal year. The year-over-year increase of up 101.5% signals a sharp rise in obligations compared with the prior year. The fiscal-year series shows that FY22 was unusually low at $16.1M, while FY23 and later years returned to higher levels, culminating in FY26 at $512M. Readers looking at contract strategy or cash flow should note the combination of many awards and a moderate average award size alongside large swings in annual obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Fca Us's federal business trended year to year?",
        "body": "Fiscal-year obligations moved from $267M in FY21 to $16.1M in FY22, then rose to $356M in FY23 and held at higher levels in FY24 ($330M) and FY25 ($254M). FY26 obligations reached $512M to date. Obligations are up 101.5% year over year. FY22 represents the low point in the series, while FY26 is the current high point to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What do award counts and sizes tell you about Fca Us's workload?",
        "body": "Fca Us received 11,836 awards in FY2026 to date, with an average award size of $43.3K. The high award count combined with that average suggests many smaller-value awards rather than a few very large contracts. The total obligations of $512M reflect the aggregate of those awards for the current fiscal year to date."
      }
